@page
@model VeSessionManager.Web.Pages.Admin.SystemSettingsModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "System Settings";
    ViewData["ActiveNav"] = "AdminSystemSettings";
    Layout = "_AppLayout";
}

<div class="page-head">
    <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Deployment-wide</p>
        <h1>System Settings</h1>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="session-panel" style="display:block;">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>PII Retention</h2></div>
    <form method="post">
        <div class="field" style="max-width:280px;">
            <label for="piiRetentionWindowDays">Retention window (days)</label>
            <input id="piiRetentionWindowDays" name="piiRetentionWindowDays" type="number" min="1" value="@Model.PiiRetentionWindowDays" placeholder="Not yet set" />
        </div>
        <p class="session-sub">Applies to <strong>candidates</strong>. Used by the PII purge job. Leave blank until an explicit value is decided — no default is assumed.</p>

        <div class="field" style="max-width:280px;margin-top:16px;">
            <label for="veContactRetentionYears">VE contact retention (years inactive)</label>
            <input id="veContactRetentionYears" name="veContactRetentionYears" type="number" min="1" value="@Model.VeContactRetentionYears" placeholder="Not yet set" />
        </div>
        <p class="session-sub">
            Applies to <strong>Volunteer Examiners</strong>. Clears email, phone, home address, Discord username and
            notes for a VE who holds no active team membership and has worked no session in this many years. Name,
            call sign, FRN, accreditations and session history are kept — that is the accreditation trail. Leave
            blank to keep contact details indefinitely; nothing is purged until a value is set. Five years is the
            documented suggestion (see docs/ve-retention.md).
        </p>

        <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:24px;"><h2>Record Retention</h2></div>
        <div class="meta-grid">
            <div class="field" style="max-width:240px;">
                <label for="auditLogRetentionDays">Audit log retention (days)</label>
                <input id="auditLogRetentionDays" name="auditLogRetentionDays" type="number" min="1" value="@Model.AuditLogRetentionDays" placeholder="Keep forever" />
            </div>
            <div class="field" style="max-width:240px;">
                <label for="jobRunHistoryRetentionDays">Job run history retention (days)</label>
                <input id="jobRunHistoryRetentionDays" name="jobRunHistoryRetentionDays" type="number" min="1" value="@Model.JobRunHistoryRetentionDays" placeholder="Keep forever" />
            </div>
            @* Blank means keep forever, like the two above — and here that may well be the right
               permanent answer rather than a placeholder: these are the legal record of what was
               filed with a VEC, and this team has had to go back to one after the fact. *@
            <div class="field" style="max-width:240px;">
                <label for="vecSubmissionArchiveRetentionDays">ARRL archive retention (days)</label>
                <input id="vecSubmissionArchiveRetentionDays" name="vecSubmissionArchiveRetentionDays" type="number" min="1" value="@Model.VecSubmissionArchiveRetentionDays" placeholder="Keep forever" />
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="session-sub">
            Both are <strong>blank by default, meaning keep everything</strong>, and nothing is deleted until you set
            a value. Neither table holds personal data &mdash; audit entries record ids, counts and configuration
            changes, never candidate names, emails or secrets &mdash; so these windows control growth, not privacy.
            <strong>Setting an audit window deletes history permanently</strong>, and the audit log is otherwise
            append-only; the job run history is operational telemetry and grows by roughly 150,000 rows a year.
        </p>

        <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:24px;"><h2>ULS Polling</h2></div>
        <div class="meta-grid">
            <div class="field" style="max-width:200px;">
                <label for="ulsWatcherStartHourEt">First check of the day (ET, 0-23)</label>
                <input id="ulsWatcherStartHourEt" name="ulsWatcherStartHourEt" type="number" min="0" max="23" value="@Model.UlsWatcherStartHourEt" required />
            </div>
            <div class="field" style="max-width:200px;">
                <label for="ulsWatcherIntervalHours">Check interval (hours)</label>
                <input id="ulsWatcherIntervalHours" name="ulsWatcherIntervalHours" type="number" min="1" value="@Model.UlsWatcherIntervalHours" required />
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="session-sub">Checks at the start hour (US Eastern) and again every interval after that — e.g. 8 + 12 checks at 8am and 8pm ET. FCC issues licenses at 2am ET Tue&ndash;Sat, so a morning check lands after that day's grants exist. Each check looks up only candidates still awaiting a grant, so it costs one request per pending applicant. <strong>These two values also drive the Renewal Monitor refresh</strong>, which reads the same FCC data through the same mirror and so runs on the same schedule.</p>

        <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:24px;"><h2>Session Ingestion</h2></div>
        <div class="field" style="max-width:280px;">
            <label for="sessionIngestionIntervalMinutes">Normal polling interval (minutes)</label>
            <input id="sessionIngestionIntervalMinutes" name="sessionIngestionIntervalMinutes" type="number" min="1" value="@Model.SessionIngestionIntervalMinutes" required />
        </div>
        <p class="session-sub">How often each team's ExamTools poll (+ Zoom/Discord/Square/email follow-up) runs. This is the cadence for every team, flat — the job itself wakes more often than this, but only polls a team once this interval has elapsed since that team's last run. To pull in a last-minute registrant right now, use <strong>Refresh candidates</strong> on the session, which does not wait for the schedule.</p>

        <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:24px;"><h2>Test Mode</h2></div>
        <div class="field" style="max-width:400px; flex-direction:row; align-items:center; gap:12px;">
            <span class="switch">
                <input id="testModeEnabled" name="testModeEnabled" type="checkbox" value="true" checked="@Model.TestModeEnabled" />
                <span class="slider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </span>
            <input name="testModeEnabled" type="hidden" value="false" />
            <label for="testModeEnabled" style="margin:0;">Test mode is on — redirect every outgoing email</label>
        </div>
        <div class="field" style="max-width:400px; margin-top:8px;">
            <label for="testModeOverrideEmail">Override email address</label>
            <input id="testModeOverrideEmail" name="testModeOverrideEmail" type="email" value="@Model.TestModeOverrideEmail" placeholder="you@example.com" />
        </div>
        <p class="session-sub">While on, every email this app would send (registration confirmations, reminders, disclosure/youth-program instructions, payment expiration notices — everything, for every team) goes to this one address instead of the real recipient, with the original recipient noted in the email itself. Use this to run a session through the full pipeline with real ExamTools data without emailing anyone for real. A red bar appears across every page while this is on.</p>

        @if (Model.UpdatedUtc is not null)
        {
            <p class="session-sub" style="margin-top:16px;">Last updated @EasternTimeFormatter.Format(Model.UpdatedUtc.Value, "MMM d, yyyy h:mm tt")</p>
        }

        <div class="panel-actions" style="align-items:flex-start; margin-top:20px;">
            <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">Save settings</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</div>

<div class="session-panel" style="display:block; margin-top:24px;">
    <div class="section-head">
        <h2>System Email</h2>
        @if (Model.IsSystemEmailConfigured)
        {
            <span class="chip chip-green">Configured</span>
        }
        else
        {
            <span class="chip chip-neutral">Not configured</span>
        }
    </div>
    <p class="session-sub">
        The deployment-wide sender for email addressed to <em>app users</em> rather than candidates —
        today that means password reset links. Candidate email (confirmations, reminders, payment
        notices) is unaffected and still sends from each team's own SMTP settings. A password reset
        can't be sent at all until this is filled in, because a system administrator may not belong to
        any team. Test mode, above, redirects these emails too.
    </p>
    <form method="post" asp-page-handler="SystemEmail">
        <div class="field" style="max-width:400px;">
            <label for="systemSmtpHost">SMTP host</label>
            <input id="systemSmtpHost" name="systemSmtpHost" value="@Model.SystemSmtpHost" placeholder="smtp.mailgun.org" />
        </div>
        <div class="field" style="max-width:200px;">
            <label for="systemSmtpPort">Port</label>
            <input id="systemSmtpPort" name="systemSmtpPort" type="number" min="1" max="65535" value="@Model.SystemSmtpPort" placeholder="587" />
        </div>
        <div class="field" style="max-width:400px;">
            <label for="systemSmtpUsername">Username</label>
            <input id="systemSmtpUsername" name="systemSmtpUsername" value="@Model.SystemSmtpUsername" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>
        <div class="field" style="max-width:400px;">
            <label for="systemSmtpPassword">Password</label>
            @* Never rendered back — an empty box means "keep the stored secret". *@
            <input id="systemSmtpPassword" name="systemSmtpPassword" type="password" autocomplete="new-password"
                   placeholder="@(Model.SystemSmtpPasswordIsSet ? "Stored — leave blank to keep" : "")" />
        </div>
        <div class="field" style="max-width:400px;">
            <p class="hint" style="margin:0;">Connections always use TLS — implicit on port 465, required STARTTLS otherwise (issue #259).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="field" style="max-width:400px;">
            <label for="systemSmtpFromAddress">From address</label>
            <input id="systemSmtpFromAddress" name="systemSmtpFromAddress" type="email" value="@Model.SystemSmtpFromAddress" placeholder="Defaults to the username" />
        </div>
        <div class="field" style="max-width:400px;">
            <label for="systemSmtpFromDisplayName">From display name</label>
            <input id="systemSmtpFromDisplayName" name="systemSmtpFromDisplayName" value="@Model.SystemSmtpFromDisplayName" placeholder="VE Ops" />
        </div>
        <div class="panel-actions" style="align-items:flex-start; margin-top:20px;">
            <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">Save email settings</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</div>

<div class="session-panel" style="display:block; margin-top:24px;">
    <div class="section-head">
        <h2>System Banner</h2>
        @if (Model.SystemBannerEnabled)
        {
            <span class="chip chip-amber">Showing</span>
        }
    </div>
    <p class="session-sub">
        A message shown across every page, for anything worth telling every signed-in user right now —
        a known FCC outage, planned maintenance, whatever comes up next. General-purpose, not tied to
        any one feature's own switch.
    </p>
    <form method="post" asp-page-handler="SystemBanner">
        <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; max-width:480px;">
            <label class="switch">
                <input id="systemBannerEnabled" name="systemBannerEnabled" type="checkbox" value="true" checked="@Model.SystemBannerEnabled"
                       data-toggle-panel="systemBannerMessageField" />
                <span class="slider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </label>
            <input name="systemBannerEnabled" type="hidden" value="false" />
            <label for="systemBannerEnabled" style="margin:0;">Show the banner</label>
        </div>
        <div id="systemBannerMessageField" style="@(Model.SystemBannerEnabled ? "" : "display:none;") margin-top:12px; max-width:480px;">
            <div class="field">
                <label for="systemBannerMessage">Message</label>
                <textarea id="systemBannerMessage" name="systemBannerMessage" rows="2">@Model.SystemBannerMessage</textarea>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="panel-actions" style="align-items:flex-start; margin-top:20px;">
            <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">Save banner</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</div>
